  "slug": "epidemic-dynamics-e923",
  "summary": "Recent preprints add opinion feedback, reinfection structure, hybrid mobility, and within-host immunity to compartmental epidemic models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is augmenting compartmental epidemic formulations with an added mechanistic layer and coupling that structure to analytical or calibration-based outputs. The agent-based study couples opinion dynamics to compartmental spread, with opinion-dependent transmission improving calibration. A chain SIR model indexes compartments by reinfection count and derives an analytical wave speed for reinfection-space traveling waves. A hybrid framework links equation-based and individual-based models through Madrid commuting networks, where mass gatherings amplify and accelerate citywide spread. A multi-scale immuno-epidemiological model connects within-host immune dynamics and symptom scores to symptomatic behavior change in influenza-like illness. The shared element is the coupling of added structure to epidemic dynamics; the novelty lies mainly in the reinfection-indexed traveling-wave formulation and opinion feedback on transmission.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-01"
}
